<title>USA: Time Warner to cut costs by $600 mln - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Time Warner to cut costs by $600 mln - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc is planning to cut costs by $600 million -- double the amount it had originally forecast -- after it completes the purchase of Turner Broadcasting System Inc, the Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said consulting firm McKinsey &amp; Co was helping Time Warner look to cut costs in all of areas, especially corporate perks like jets and resort homes.</p>
<p>Although Time Warner declined to comment, it quoted &quot;people close&quot; to the company as saying it had been under pressure from Ted Turner to reduce its debt and cut costs.</p>
<p>The U.S. Federal Communications Commission has approved the merger, which is expected to close Thursday, it added.</p>
